The ledger stall sits wedged between a water-rationing queue and a shuttered fuel kiosk. The woman behind it looks up from a column of figures, pencil still moving for one more line. "Vey," she says. "Nobody calls me Tamsin unless they owe me or want something." Her eyes drop to your hands, then to the comm tag at your collar. "The Kestrel name. The foreman's been asking after you all morning."

