Vey sets the pencil down. She looks at you for a long moment, then at the queue behind you, then at the shuttered kiosk. "Nobody's asked me that before," she says. "Usually they ask what I'll charge." She turns the ledger a quarter-turn on the counter, away from the queue. "Why me? Plenty of brokers on this rock."

*If you want to make her answer count, this would be a Make a Connection.*

