A hauler with a fuel-stained collar studies your credits, then the queue, and takes them. He says the raiders were last seen off the sealed plant's lane, running dark. He says they knew his convoy's schedule and the family names aboard. Behind him, two fuel hands stop talking and drift toward the water line. Vey stays shut behind her ledger, but a man at the queue's edge is now watching you count out the rest.

